        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "89fbf7ce-f81b-51be-ad39-589c4dc660e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon, French Parliament\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon, Olivier Ferrand\n- Concepts: mutualism, federalism, anarchist philosophy, property\n- Works: What Is Property?\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- What Is Property? is a nonfiction work by Pierre-Joseph Proudhon about property and its relation to anarchist philosophy, and it was first published in 1840.\n- After the 1848 revolution, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and then referred to himself as a federalist.\n- Cercle Proudhon was founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Proudhon.\n- Olivier Ferrand was elected to the French Parliament in June 2012.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
